  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5011",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the pathogenesis of HCC1937 through multiple mechanistic pathways, with the compound acting as a target for several pharmacologically distinct agents. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin interacts with P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, a compound that in turn targets HCC1937. Similarly, doxorubicin also interacts with GDM-1, which is targeted by the same compound, reinforcing the role of this agent in the pathophysiology of HCC1937. Additionally, doxorubicin is linked to palmarumycin CP18, another compound that directly targets HCC1937. These findings collectively suggest that doxorubicin may exert its effects on HCC1937 through the activation of P2X purinoceptors or through the action of a specific inhibitor of the P2X receptor family. The consistent involvement of a common target, [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, across multiple pathways underscores the potential for a shared mechanism of action in the context of HCC1937. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between doxorubicin and HCC1937, though further validation through in vivo studies is required to confirm the clinical relevance of these findings.",
